│ Review title: Paracetamol (acetaminophen) with or without an antiemetic for acute migraine headaches in adults       │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Review background:                                                                                                   │
│ This is an updated version of the original Cochrane review published in Issue 11, 2010 (Derry 2010). Migraine is a   │
│ common, disabling condition and a burden for the individual, health services and society. Many sufferers choose not  │
│ to, or are unable to, seek professional help and rely on over‐the‐counter analgesics. Co‐therapy with an antiemetic  │
│ should help to reduce nausea and vomiting, which are commonly associated with migraine.                              │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Review objective:                                                                                                    │
│ To determine the efficacy and tolerability of paracetamol (acetaminophen), alone or in combination with an           │
│ antiemetic, compared with placebo and other active interventions in the treatment of acute migraine in adults.       │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Selection criteria:                                                                                                  │
